      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the smallest positive \\( x \\) such that the sum \\( x + 5678 \\) results in a palindrome, let's analyze the properties of palindromes. A palindrome reads the same forward and backward. The easiest way to generate palindromes is by starting from the middle and expanding outward.\n\nSince the task requires \\( x + 5678 \\) to be a palindrome and we are looking for the smallest \\( x \\), let's start by considering the simplest palindromes, such as \\( 0 \\), \\( 1 \\), \\( 22 \\), etc.\n\n1. If \\( x = 0 \\):\n   \\[\n   0 + 5678 = 5678\n   \\]\n   5678 is not a palindrome.\n\n2. If \\( x = 1 \\):\n   \\[\n   1 + 5678 = 5679\n   \\]\n   5679 is not a palindrome.\n\n3. If \\( x = 10 \\):\n   \\[\n   10 + 5678 = 5688\n   \\]\n   5688 is not a palindrome.\n\n4. If \\( x = 11 \\):\n   \\[\n   11 + 5678 = 5689\n   \\]\n   5689 is a palindrome. Since 5689 is greater than 5678, it satisfies the requirement of being a palindrome.\n\nThus, the smallest \\( x \\) that satisfies the condition \\( x + 5678 \\) being a palindrome is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).",
